<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>

<!--
  The button bar layout this mod ships as its default.

  Read only when the player has no layout of their own. The moment they arrange the bar in the UI options
  page their arrangement is written to UIOverhaul_ButtonBar.xml in RimWorld's config folder, and this file
  stops being consulted. Editing it changes what a new player sees, not what an existing one has.

  The root element and the entry shape match what the options page writes, so this file can be copied
  straight into the config folder and hand-edited from there if that is ever useful.

  Order here is the order on the bar. Anything not listed is appended AFTER everything that is, which is
  why every tab that ships with the game or its expansions is named below even where its position is not
  interesting: leaving one out would push it past the pause menu.

  The UI options button is not listed and cannot be. It is drawn at the far right of the bar, outside the
  entry list entirely, so it is always last no matter what this file says. The pause menu is therefore the
  last entry here, which puts it immediately to the left of that button.

  mode values are Default, Minimize, TextOnly and Maximize. Default honors a def's own request to be
  minimized, which is why Factions, Ideoligions and History arrive as bare icons; Maximize overrides that
  and gives them their labels like every other tab.
-->
<ButtonBar>

  <entry><tab>Architect</tab></entry>

  <!-- This mod's tab. It answers the question asked before opening anything else: who needs attention. -->
  <entry><tab>Gideon_Pawns</tab></entry>

  <entry><tab>Animals</tab></entry>

  <!-- Also this mod's. -->
  <entry><tab>GZP_GrowZones</tab></entry>

  <!-- Dimensions RePocketed. Skipped without that mod, so listing it is free. -->
  <entry><tab>KB_PocketDimension_Tab</tab></entry>

  <entry><tab>Quests</tab></entry>

  <!-- These three ask to be minimized in their own defs. Maximize gives them labels instead. -->
  <entry>
    <tab>Factions</tab>
    <mode>Maximize</mode>
  </entry>

  <!-- This mod's, standing where Ideology's own button did. Skipped without the expansion, which is what
       IdeoTabs.Available answers: with no Ideology this entry is suppressed and vanilla's is too, so the bar
       simply has no ideoligions button, exactly as it would without the mod. -->
  <entry>
    <tab>Gideon_Ideoligions</tab>
    <mode>Maximize</mode>
  </entry>

  <entry>
    <tab>History</tab>
    <mode>Maximize</mode>
  </entry>

  <entry><tab>World</tab></entry>

  <!--
    The rest of the game's tabs. Named only so they land before the pause menu rather than after it; their
    order among themselves is vanilla's own. Move them wherever suits.

    Inspect appears only while something is selected, and Mechs needs Biotech and a mechanitor, so neither
    is usually on screen. Entries naming a def that is not loaded are skipped and left alone.
  -->
  <entry><tab>Inspect</tab></entry>
  <entry><tab>Wildlife</tab></entry>
  <entry><tab>Research</tab></entry>
  <entry><tab>Mechs</tab></entry>

  <!--
    The pause menu, pinned to the end.

    <last> is what guarantees the position. Naming every tab above fixes the order of the ones we know
    about, but the bar appends any MainButtonDef the layout does not mention, so a tab from a mod nobody
    has heard of would otherwise land to the right of the menu. This entry is held back until those
    appends are in, which puts it immediately left of the UI options button whatever else is installed.
  -->
  <entry>
    <tab>Menu</tab>
    <last>true</last>
  </entry>

  <!--
    Hidden by default, because the pawns tab covers what they do.

    Work priorities, the daily schedule and the assignment policies are all reachable from a colonist's row
    there, which makes three separate tabs for the same three things redundant on a fresh install.

    Hiding is not removing. Every one of these is still offered in the UI options page's bar editor under
    "Not on the bar", and adding a tab takes it back off this list, so a player who wants the vanilla tabs
    back has them in two clicks with no file editing.
  -->
  <hidden>
    <li>Work</li>
    <li>Schedule</li>
    <li>Assign</li>
  </hidden>

</ButtonBar>
